cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Senescence enhancer reproducibility: code, derived results and
  provenance records
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite both the preprint and the
  Zenodo deposition of the large artifacts.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gabriel
    family-names: Kim
    affiliation: Stanford University
    email: gabeykim@stanford.edu
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/gabeykim/senescence-enhancer-reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Code, derived result tables, publication figures and provenance records
  for a study of whether senescence-associated enhancer activity is
  reproducible enough to model, and how far a sequence-to-activity model
  can be pushed toward designing a senescence-responsive element.
  Replicative senescence shows no reproducible H3K27ac programme: the
  cleanest within-replicative comparison available, with no technical
  confound, is Spearman +0.054, against a within-OIS ceiling of +0.653.
  A head trained on Borzoi trunk embeddings reaches Spearman +0.5484 on a
  cross-lab, cross-tissue holdout, which is 86.1 percent of the measured
  +0.637 reproducibility ceiling. Motif insertion saturates at 0.773 times
  the change required to move a sequence from the median to the 95th
  percentile of predicted activity. Every H3K27ac dataset used has at most
  two replicates per arm, which bounds every result reported.
keywords:
  - senescence
  - enhancer
  - reproducibility
  - genomics
  - chromatin
  - deep-learning
  - cis-regulatory-elements
  - H3K27ac
  - oncogene-induced senescence
license: MIT
